    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d401">

                <pb facs="0375" n="367" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg367"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/1584</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Under Secretary of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-28">June 28, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Australian Minister called upon me at quarter past one today, the only time I
                    had available to see him. He left with me the attached memorandum<anchor n="84"
                        xml:id="d401-f1"/> which he said represented the views of his Government as
                    urgently expressed to him in telegrams which he had received during the past
                    twenty-four hours.</p>
                <p>The Minister stated that he was due to see the Secretary of State, together with
                    the British Ambassador, at four o’clock this afternoon. I told the Minister I
                    would be glad to see that the Secretary had this memorandum before the
                    meeting.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
